&lt;p class=MsoNormal style='margin-right:-.5in;text-align:justify;line-height:
18.0pt'>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>                  In Daniel &lt;b>2&lt;/b>:44 &lt;i>those
kings&lt;/i> [&lt;/span>&lt;span lang=HE dir=RTL style='font-size:12.0pt'>מ&lt;/span>&lt;span
lang=HE dir=RTL style='font-size:14.0pt'>ֶלֶךְ&lt;/span>&lt;span dir=LTR>&lt;/span>&lt;span
style='font-size:12.0pt'>&lt;span dir=LTR>&lt;/span>] seems to refer to the preceding
four &lt;u>kingdoms&lt;/u> [&lt;/span>&lt;span lang=HE dir=RTL style='font-size:12.0pt'>מַלְכוּ&lt;/span>&lt;span
dir=LTR>&lt;/span>&lt;span style='font-size:12.0pt'>&lt;span dir=LTR>&lt;/span>] of &lt;b>2&lt;/b>:38-43.
Daniel uses &lt;i>kingdom&lt;/i> and &lt;i>king&lt;/i> somewhat interchangeably in that &lt;i>king&lt;/i>
can by metonymy stand for the realm he rules, even though over a period of time
there may be several kings in one kingdom. In &lt;b>2&lt;/b>:39 the writer says, &lt;i>“And
after &lt;u>you&lt;/u>, Nebuchadnezzar, will arise &lt;u>another kingdom&lt;/u> inferior to
&lt;u>you&lt;/u>.”&lt;/i> A similar shift of terms comes in &lt;b>2&lt;/b>:44, &lt;i>“In the days
of those &lt;u>kings&lt;/u> the God of heaven will set up a kingdom . . . it will
break all these &lt;u>kingdoms&lt;/u> in pieces and consume (them).”&lt;/i> Later in &lt;b>7&lt;/b>:17
the four beasts from the sea (&lt;b>7&lt;/b>:3; earth, &lt;b>7&lt;/b>:17) are said to
represent four &lt;u>kings&lt;/u>, whereas &lt;b>7&lt;/b>:23 says that &lt;i>“the fourth beast
will be a fourth &lt;u>kingdom&lt;/u> that will be different from all the &lt;u>kingdoms&lt;/u>.”
&lt;/i>&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>APPROACHING THE MILLENNIAL ISSUE WITH MINISTRY IN MIND</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/future-things-eschatology/approaching-the-millennial-issue-with-ministry-in-mind/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/future-things-eschatology/approaching-the-millennial-issue-with-ministry-in-mind/</guid><description>&lt;style>
